cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "3MF Bio: an open schema for recording biofabrication end to end"
message: "If you use this specification or its validators, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  An open schema, built on the 3MF package format, for recording biofabrication
  work end to end in a single file: material identity and synthesis route, cell
  provenance and authentication, formulation and rheology, print process across
  twenty modalities, deposition heads and nozzles, calibration events, staged
  post-print maturation with bioreactor and stimulation regimes, and assay
  batteries measured over a timecourse. Its organising constraint is that every
  numeric parameter must declare where its value came from, enforced by XML
  Schema, ISO Schematron and a reference validator. It is not a standard and
  asserts no acceptance thresholds; it supplies the fields so that laboratories
  and manufacturers can record against their own criteria.
